  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Modelling Inclusive Education in Tanzania</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Education has the power to transform disabled children&apos;s lives. In Tanzania only an estimated 3% - 5% of disabled children go to school and many of these are in special schools. In 2010, the government in Tanzania approved a progressive new national strategy for inclusive education. This application will help the government test implementation of the strategy in one province. By working with children, families, schools and government agencies it will tackle common barriers to disabled children&apos;s participation in school - lack of resources, teachers that are not trained or aware of the needs of disabled children, and discrimination from family and community members. As a result, more disabled children will be able to attend mainstream school alongside their non-disabled peers.</narrative>
  </description>
